{
  "name": "audit5 PROTO: a smart contract as the caller of claim, on the Go VM. The caller is the Go VM's own paymaster test contract (audit5/paymaster.wasm, from mx-chain-vm-go v1.6.0 test/paymaster): forwardExecution(relayer, dest, endpoint) pays the first payment to the relayer and sends the rest to dest.endpoint in an async call; on success it forwards what came back to the original caller. One paymaster is payable by smart contracts, the other is not: both claims succeed, because a payout with no function to the contract that is calling is a back transfer, which the VM delivers without a payable check (mx-chain-vm-go vmhost/contexts/output.go, isBackTransferWithoutExecution). No code of the caller runs inside claim; the caller gets the payout and the key.",
